  "notes": "{発掘|はっくつ} primarily means archaeological excavation, but is also commonly used figuratively for discovering hidden talent or facts.\n\nWRITING:\n- {発|はつ} (emit, emit, departure)\n- {掘|くつ} (dig)\n\nUSAGE:\n- {発掘|はっくつ}する (to excavate, to discover - suru verb)\n- {発掘|はっくつ}{調査|ちょうさ} (excavation survey)\n- {発掘|はっくつ}{現場|げんば} (excavation site)\n- Entertainment: finding new artists or performers\n- Business: discovering hidden talent in the workforce\n- Journalism: uncovering previously unknown information\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {遺跡|いせき}の{発掘|はっくつ} (excavation of ruins)\n- {人材|じんざい}{発掘|はっくつ} (talent discovery)\n- {新人|しんじん}{発掘|はっくつ} (discovering newcomers)\n- {発掘|はっくつ}{品|ひん} (excavated items)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {採掘|さいくつ} (mining, extraction)\n- {掘削|くっさく} (drilling, excavation)\n- {考古学|こうこがく} (archaeology)\n- {発見|はっけん} (discovery)",
